BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev_elissa_sail250-2026-08-08@coast-guide
DTSTAMP:20260808T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260808
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260810
SUMMARY:1877 Tall Ship ELISSA — free deck tours
DESCRIPTION:A National Historic Landmark square-rigged iron barque\, and o
 ne of only three ships of her kind left in the world that still actively 
 sails. Pensacola is the FIRST stop on her Sail250 voyage for the nation's
  250th — and only her third recorded visit ever\, after 1886 and 2018. 
 Walking her deck costs nothing. A ship-and-history kid gets rigging and 1
 49 years of iron\; the stroller rolls the pier.\nPrice: Free\nDrive: 25 m
 in from Gulf Breeze\nTimes: Fri 8/7 – Sun 8/9 · free self-guided deck 
 tours (hours vary by day — see watch-outs)\nChecked against the venue's
  own page on 2026-08-05\nhttps://grayhicks.github.io/coast-guide/events/e
 v-elissa-sail250.html
LOCATION:Palafox Pier\, 895 S Palafox St\, Pensacola\, FL 32502
URL:https://grayhicks.github.io/coast-guide/events/ev-elissa-sail250.html
END:VEVENT
